    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvnw test` build passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature end-to-end for `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), following the project's OfficeFloor + generated-DTO conventions.\n\n**What the spec required:** when a request includes an ISO `birthDate`, return `ageBand` derived against the owner's `registrationDate` \u2014 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`OwnerAgeBand.java`** (new helper, matching the `OwnerCheckDigit` pattern) \u2014 single source of truth that computes the band from `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, returning `null` when no birth date is present.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a read-time `ageBand` mapping (like `checkDigit`, `locality`, etc.). `birthDate` maps from the request DTO to the entity automatically by name, so it's stored at creation and the band is derived at read time against the effective registration date.\n\nThe test posts `birthDate: \"1990-01-01\"` (registration defaults to today, 2026-10-01 \u2192 age 36) and asserts `ageBand == \"ADULT\"` \u2014 passing.\n\nNote: the `birthDate` ends up stored only via the Spring Data JPA path (the active test profile); the JDBC repository impl does manual SQL and wasn't touched, so if you later exercise the `jdbc` profile its insert/select would need the column added too \u2014 let me know if you want that covered.",
