    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change mirrors the codebase's established convention for derived read-time fields and lands each piece in its natural home.\n\n- `OwnerAgeBand` is a direct structural twin of the existing `OwnerCheckDigit`: `final` class, private constructor, \"single source of truth\" javadoc, an `ageBand(Owner)` accessor that delegates to a pure `ageBand(LocalDate, LocalDate)` helper \u2014 exactly the `checkDigit(Owner)` \u2192 `luhn(String)` split already in the tree. The second overload is not speculative here; it's the same entity-accessor/pure-logic separation the sibling class uses, and it keeps the date arithmetic independent of the `Owner` entity.\n- The mapper wiring (`@Named(\"ageBand\")` delegating to the function class, plus the `@Mapping` line) is identical in shape to `checkDigit`/`identityKey`, so the logic stays out of the mapper and in the function unit where this codebase keeps it.\n- `birthDate` is a plain persisted field with a conventional getter/setter on `Owner`, and the derived `ageBand` correctly gets no column \u2014 consistent with the \"derived at read time, needs no column\" rationale.\n- Schema changes are applied uniformly across all four dialects, and the OpenAPI additions are placed correctly (writable `birthDate` on the request fields, `readOnly` `ageBand` on the response) with descriptions that match the spec's semantics.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accretion \u2014 a maintainer would find this natural.",
